    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0350" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washburn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-21T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 22—7:07
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Department’s telegram 3, January 18, 7 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >p.m.</hi>]<anchor n="97" xml:id="d166-f1"/> Foreign Office states that
                    requests made by Legation in pursuance of Department’s telegram 23, December 22,
                    3 p.m.,<anchor n="98" xml:id="d166-f2"/> will be granted and that written reply
                    to Legation’s note will be forthcoming without delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washburn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
